    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0540" n="444" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg444"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Governor Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In view of the absence of the Italian consul from his post at New Orleans, the
                    Italian Government has provisionally appointed Marquis <pb facs="0541" n="445"
                        xml:id="pg445"/> Camillo Romano, second secretary of the embassy, to be
                    gerant of the consulate.</p>
                <p>He has been recognized in that capacity by direction of the President. I have the
                    honor to advise you thereof, and at the request of the Italian chargé to ask
                    that Signor Romano be accorded due recognition and all possible consideration by
                    the authorities of Louisiana.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
